---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const { names } = Astro.props as { names: Record<string, string> };
const base = '/participation-demographic-counts/20261107-01/';
type Composition = { estimated_current_group_count: number;
	reported_current_choice_counts: Record<string, number | null> };
type Row = { state_code: string; contest_code: string; subset: { sub: number; longName: string };
	estimated_current_group_count: number; population_match: { group_share_pct_of_current_electorate: number };
	composition: Record<string, Composition>;
	sensitivity_scenarios: { reported_opposite_party_counts: Record<string, number | null> }[] };
type Jurisdiction = { state_code: string; qualified_group_comparisons: number };
const review: { estimates: Row[]; jurisdictions: Jurisdiction[] } = JSON.parse(
	readFileSync(`public${base}demographic-current-counts.json`, 'utf8'));
const count = (value: number | null) => value === null ? 'Unavailable'
	: (Math.round(value / 1000) * 1000).toLocaleString('en-US');
const office: Record<string, string> = { SG: 'Senate', GG: 'Governor', HG: 'House' };
const states = new Set(review.estimates.filter(r => r.state_code !== 'US').map(r => r.state_code)).size;
const codes = ['US', ...review.jurisdictions.filter(r => r.qualified_group_comparisons > 0).map(r => r.state_code)];
const range = (row: Row, prior: string) => {
	const values = row.sensitivity_scenarios.flatMap(s => s.reported_opposite_party_counts[prior] === null
		? [] : [s.reported_opposite_party_counts[prior] as number]);
	return values.length ? `${count(Math.min(...values))}–${count(Math.max(...values))}` : 'Unavailable';
};
---

<section id="participation-demographic-counts" aria-labelledby="demographic-counts-title">
	<h3 id="demographic-counts-title">Demographic switching: preliminary counts</h3>
	<p><strong>{review.estimates.length} qualified group comparisons across {states} states plus national House.</strong>
		These separate scenarios use each contest's actual published demographic population shares and
		its matching subgroup's joint recalled-2024/current-2026 choices. They are conditional estimates,
		not observed headcounts or causal persuasion.</p>
	<p>Estimated current group = N26 × g; reported opposite-party choice = N26 × g × q × p.
		N26 is UF Election Lab's <strong>Initial Estimate</strong> of ballots; g is the published current-group
		share, q its recalled prior-choice share and p current choice within that prior group.
		The reference assumes these response shares represent all ballot-casters. Some choices remain
		pre-election responses after unsuccessful recontact.</p>
	<p><strong>Group drop-off remains unavailable:</strong> corresponding 2024 demographic coalition
		baselines are missing. These counts do not supply demographic turnout rates, percentages of the
		original Trump/Harris group, or shares of overall swing. Demographics describe current voters,
		not an unchanged 2024 cohort.</p>
	{codes.map(code => {
		const rows = review.estimates.filter(r => r.state_code === code);
		return <details class="explorer-notes" open={code === 'US'} data-demographic-jurisdiction={code}>
			<summary>{names[code]} · {rows.length} qualified group comparisons</summary>
			<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${names[code]} demographic switching counts`}>
				<table><caption>Counts rounded to 1,000. Rounded zero does not establish zero switching.
					Stress ranges are not confidence intervals. Never sum overlapping groups, offices or national/state estimates.</caption>
					<thead><tr><th scope="col">2026 contest / current group</th><th scope="col">Published group share</th>
						<th scope="col">Estimated current group</th><th scope="col">Reported Trump → D</th>
						<th scope="col">Reported Harris → R</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>{rows.map(row => <tr data-demographic-state={code} data-demographic-contest={row.contest_code} data-demographic-subset={row.subset.sub}>
						<th scope="row">{office[row.contest_code]} / {row.subset.longName}</th>
						<td data-demographic-share>{row.population_match.group_share_pct_of_current_electorate}%</td>
						<td data-demographic-population>{count(row.estimated_current_group_count)}</td>
						<td data-demographic-trump-flow>{count(row.composition.R.reported_current_choice_counts.D)}
							<br /><small>Stress: {range(row, 'R')}</small></td>
						<td data-demographic-harris-flow>{count(row.composition.D.reported_current_choice_counts.R)}
							<br /><small>Stress: {range(row, 'D')}</small></td>
					</tr>)}</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${names[code]} demographic prior presidential composition counts`}>
				<table><caption>Prior presidential nonvote does not establish first-ever participation,
					all-race nonvoting, eligibility entry or an identified returning voter. Suppressed choices remain unavailable.</caption>
					<thead><tr><th scope="col">2026 contest / current group</th><th scope="col">No 2024 presidential vote</th>
						<th scope="col">2026 D / R from that group</th><th scope="col">Other 2024 presidential choice</th>
						<th scope="col">2026 D / R from that group</th></tr></thead>
					<tbody>{rows.map(row => <tr data-demographic-composition-state={code} data-demographic-composition-contest={row.contest_code} data-demographic-composition-subset={row.subset.sub}>
						<th scope="row">{office[row.contest_code]} / {row.subset.longName}</th>
						<td>{count(row.composition.N.estimated_current_group_count)}</td>
						<td>{count(row.composition.N.reported_current_choice_counts.D)} / {count(row.composition.N.reported_current_choice_counts.R)}</td>
						<td>{count(row.composition.O.estimated_current_group_count)}</td>
						<td data-demographic-other-flows>{count(row.composition.O.reported_current_choice_counts.D)} / {count(row.composition.O.reported_current_choice_counts.R)}</td>
					</tr>)}</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</details>;
	})}
	<p class="caption">Stress varies estimated totals by −5%, 0 and +5%, and transfers −2, 0 or +2 recalled
		composition points from Harris to Trump. The archive separately includes half-point rounding
		envelopes in g, q and p; neither method supplies design-aware uncertainty. Percentages are not
		renormalized. The 18–44 category uses its exact published question, not summed rounded age bins.</p>
	<p>Age groups overlap, as do race and White-education groups. No county/precinct estimates or voting-mode
		weights are inferred here. National House excludes unsampled D.C. and uses 123,267,000 estimated
		ballots across the 50 states; complete native national and D.C. observations remain in the archive.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Demographic-count coverage: all 50 states and D.C.</summary>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Demographic count coverage">
			<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Jurisdiction</th><th scope="col">Qualified group comparisons / next evidence</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{review.jurisdictions.map(row => <tr data-demographic-coverage={row.state_code}>
					<th scope="row">{names[row.state_code]}</th><td>{row.qualified_group_comparisons
						? `${row.qualified_group_comparisons} comparisons; acquire historical group coalitions and linked turnout`
						: 'Acquire applicable qualified joint cells and matched demographic population shares; no allocation'}</td>
				</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<p class="caption">Turnout inputs: Michael McDonald, University of Florida Election Lab, CSV v0.2 and
		documentation v0.1, CC BY 4.0, unchanged. Derived analysis is not endorsed by UF, SSRS or CNN.
		Complete selected published facts, source hashes, all dispositions, native licensed turnout inputs,
		methods, exact code and tests are included. No individual records or restricted NORC materials.</p>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete demographic counts + selected inputs + code (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}demographic-current-counts.json`} download>Exact demographic counts + sensitivity + exclusions (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Demographic archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-demographic-counts { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
